WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:02.500
Who survived the battle for Hometree?

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Is Jake now the leader of the Na'Vi people?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.842
We break down the ending of "Avatar" before
"The Way of Water" premieres!

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.529
"Avatar" takes place in 2154.

00:00:11.529 --> 00:00:16.670
Humans have depleted the Earth's natural resources
and moved on to outer space, colonizing worlds

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:21.580
like Pandora, a moon orbiting a gas giant
in the Alpha Centauri galaxy.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.310
The main character is Jake Sully, a paraplegic
former Marine.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.330
His identical twin brother was part of a team
of scientists on Pandora who are researching

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.660
the planet and its indigenous inhabitants,
the Na'Vi.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.469
Using human-Na'vi hybrids called avatars,
humans can walk among the Na'vi, communicate

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:39.540
with them, and learn their ways.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.680
Jake joins Dr. Grace Augustine, scientist
Norm Spellman, and Marine pilot Trudy on their

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.680
research mission.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.600
Of course, the Resources Development Administration
has more in mind.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.380
As RDA administrator Parker Selfridge points
out, the real reason humans are on Pandora

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.719
is to mine a mineral called unobtanium, which
sells for millions on Earth.

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:03.280
Colonel Miles Quaritch offers Jake a deal:
Find out all he can about the Na'vi, and he'll

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.510
make sure Jake gets new legs.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:09.020
But Jake's "infiltration" into the Na'vi civilization
doesn't go as he expected.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.550
He meets a Na'vi woman named Neytiri, learns
about the planet and the Na'vi's spiritual

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.670
connection to all living things, and becomes
one of them.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:21.119
Jake and Neytiri fall in love and become lifemates
— complicated by the fact that Jake is still

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:25.329
a human, living vicariously through his Na'vi
avatar, and the fact that he's technically

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:27.077
a spy for the RDA.

00:01:28.059 --> 00:01:29.731
"I trusted you.

00:01:30.294 --> 00:01:31.774
I trusted you!"

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.101
Toward the end of "Avatar," the RDA orders
the destruction of Hometree, Neytiri's tribe's

00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:44.270
home base, because of the rich deposit of
unobtainium that lies beneath.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.189
By this point, Jake is fully on team Na'vi,
even though Neytiri and other members of her

00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:51.490
tribe have turned against him after finding
out about his spying.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:55.829
Jake has completely changed his identity,
considering himself a part of the Na'vi, embracing

00:01:55.829 --> 00:01:59.189
their beliefs, and so he fights for their
cause against the RDA.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:03.600
But Quartich's huge military planes, massive
guns, and numerous soldiers quickly overpower

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.170
the tribe, and Hometree is destroyed.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.560
During the battle, many lives are lost, including
Neytriri's father, Eytukan.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.700
Jake, Grace, and Norm's human bodies are rescued
by Trudy, who airlifts them and their avatar

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.930
capsules to a safe location, while their Na'vi
avatars are left in the forest.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.019
But during the mayhem, Quartich shoots them,
with a bullet hitting Grace.

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:28.060
To regain the trust of Neytiri, the Omaticaya
tribe, and their new chief Tsu'tey, Jake mounts

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:33.209
and bonds with Taruk, a huge dragon-like beast
related to the smaller banshees.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:37.600
By bonding with this fierce beast, whom the
Na'vi both revere and fear, Jake proves that

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.667
he's a part of the Na'vi, that he respects
their culture, and he wants to live among them.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:46.440
Jake is embraced by Neytiri, her mother Mo'at,
and Tsu'tey, and together they make plans

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:51.450
to gather the numerous Na'vi tribes to fight
back against the RDA and evict them from Pandora.

00:02:51.632 --> 00:02:57.170
Before Jake sets out to unite the Na'vi clans,
he has one request of Mo'at: Save Grace.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.501
Still suffering from her gunshot wound, Grace's
life is in the Na'vi's hands, as is the life

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:02.590
of her avatar.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:07.640
As Neytiri explains, all life on Pandora is
connected via a biological neural network,

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.510
though the Na'vi consider it more of a spiritual
connection than a scientific one.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:15.810
The Tree of Voices allows living Na'vi to
hear the memories of their ancestors, while

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:20.730
the Tree of Souls is said to be the closest
connection to Eywa, the guiding force of Pandora

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.260
that the Na'vi worship as a deity.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.230
The Tree of Souls, Neytiri explains, has such
power that it can transfer her consciousness

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:31.760
through the immersive neural network of Pandora
and have her permanently placed into her avatar

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.510
body so she can survive.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.260
This transformation doesn't just highlight
the Na'vi's spiritual beliefs but also hints

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.900
at the potential scientific advancements that
could be achieved in the future.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.569
Grace's body is weak, and she doesn't survive
the process.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:48.450
But before she dies, she assures Jake that
she sees Eywa, the connections are real, and

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.280
the world of Pandora is truly a living thing.

00:03:52.516 --> 00:03:53.753
"I'm with her Jake.

00:03:56.243 --> 00:03:57.271
She's real."

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:04.090
The final battle for Pandora includes the
RDA soldiers, the many tribes of Pandora,

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.860
and one final participant: Eywa herself.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:10.980
Or, at least, Eywa manifested through the
animals and wildlife of Pandora, who came

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.090
to the Na'vi's defense at the last minute.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:17.010
The night before the battle, Jake connects
neurologically to the Tree of Souls and asks

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.000
that Eywa help them on their quest to defeat
the RDA.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.800
This, more than his bond with Toruk, proves
Jake has fully embraced his life as a Na'vi.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.530
He used Toruk to regain Neytiri and the other
Na'vi's trust, but his prayer to Eywa is a

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:34.427
private act, showing us that he now believes
in the power of Pandora and its spiritual network.

00:04:34.427 --> 00:04:38.610
During the battle, at a moment when it looks
like the Na'vi might be defeated once again,

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:42.060
suddenly a great rumble is heard from beyond
the forest.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.800
Numerous animals from throughout the planet
join the fight, understanding that the RDA

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.110
is destroying their world and their survival
depends on their involvement.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:52.920
Not only is the neural connection on Pandora
more significant than previously thought,

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.900
but the creatures of the planet are capable
of more complex decisions.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.630
"Eywa has heard you!"

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:04.000
The animals joining the fight eventually lead
to the RDA's defeat and the return of Pandora

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.000
to its original inhabitants.

00:05:06.206 --> 00:05:10.729
After the battle, many of the humans left
on Pandora are forced to head back to Earth.

00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:14.510
Jake, of course, wants to stay, but he can't
do so while still in his human body.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.560
The love between Jake and Neytiri is strong,
but with humans unable to breathe Pandora's

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.919
air, maintaining their relationship would
be rather difficult.

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:25.710
Not to mention the fact that Jake doesn't
even consider himself human anymore.

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:29.340
He's spent so much time as one of the Na'vi,
learning and embracing their way of life,

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.740
that remaining human would just be a letdown.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.840
So Jake asks the Na'vi to connect his human
body as well as his Na'vi avatar to the Tree

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.910
of Souls via their neural networks.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:42.030
The Na'vi pray together, chant, and ask that
Eywa transfer Jake from his human form into

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:43.030
his avatar.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.699
The closing shot of the film is Jake's avatar
opening his eyes urgently, suggesting that

00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:51.482
the process did indeed work and that Jake
can now go on living as a true Na'vi.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:56.199
Sigourney Weaver's Dr. Grace Augustine doesn't
survive the battle of Hometree, and she was

00:05:56.199 --> 00:05:58.210
far from the only casualty.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.100
During the epic final conflict, Trudy switches
sides as well, outfitting her fighter plane

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.210
and face with Na'vi colors, but her plane
gets shot down.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:10.250
Omaticaya chief Tsu'tey is also mortally wounded
in the battle, and after the battle ends,

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.620
asks Jake to end his suffering.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:16.210
At first, Jake is reluctant to do so, but
as Tsu'tey explains, it is a great honor,

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:19.960
and passes the tribe leadership on to Jake,
before Jake ends his suffering.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.290
On the human front, scientist Norm Spellman
survives the battle.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:27.509
Unfortunately, his Na'vi avatar gets shot
and dies, so Norm has to remain in his human

00:06:27.509 --> 00:06:29.650
form on Pandora from then on.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:34.120
Norm is one of the few humans who is permitted
to stay, and he fronts a new and ongoing scientific

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:38.520
exploration team — one that has nothing
to do with procuring unobtainium or conquering

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.380
the indigenous peoples of the planet.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:45.240
Neytiri's mother Mo'at also survives the final
battle, and it's she who supervises the ritual

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:49.858
at the Tree of Souls to transfer Jake's consciousness
from his human body to his Na'vi avatar.

00:06:50.089 --> 00:06:55.139
Greedy RDA administrator Parker Selfridge
was only out for one thing: the money and

00:06:55.139 --> 00:06:58.510
power that came with dominating the Na'vi
and destroying their land.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:02.720
As a character, Selfridge was the movie's
embodiment of colonialist and imperialist

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.280
capitalist interests.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:09.009
His descriptions of the Na'vi as, quote, "fly-bitten
savages" that live in trees could mirror any

00:07:09.009 --> 00:07:13.330
of history's conquering forces as they dominated
the indigenous peoples in various countries

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.710
across the world.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:18.449
Thankfully, Selfridge is banished from Pandora
by the end of the film, though it isn't known

00:07:18.449 --> 00:07:20.660
whether he's learned any kind of lesson.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:24.990
A much more gruesome fate befalls Colonel
Miles Quaritch, who throughout the movie becomes

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:28.710
a more sinister, violent, and frightening
villain than Selfridge.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.530
During the final battle, Quaritch heads to
the Hallelujah mountains where Jake's human

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.389
body is connected to his Na'vi avatar through
the pod.

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:39.050
Quaritch tries to disconnect and kill Jake,
but his mission is interrupted by Neytiri

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:43.800
riding her new thanator, a fierce land mammal
of Pandora that looks like a cross between

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.539
a cat and a dinosaur.

00:07:45.539 --> 00:07:49.410
Just as Quaritch is about to crush Jake with
the use of his AMP suit, Neytiri launches

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.759
two giant arrows into his chest.

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:56.370
It's after Quaritch's death that Neytiri meets
Jake's human form for the first time, lovingly

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.846
greeting each other with the traditional Na'vi
saying:

00:07:58.846 --> 00:08:00.936
"I see you."

00:08:02.626 --> 00:08:04.716
"I see you."

00:08:04.837 --> 00:08:09.370
"Avatar" was so successful, and James Cameron
became so immersed in its world-building,

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:13.210
that it's no surprise there are plans for
a whopping four additional movies.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:17.830
But with or without all of the upcoming sequels,
James Cameron's "Avatar" was a truly innovative

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:23.100
and interesting film, one that plunged audiences
deep into a new world and heralded a new era

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.100
of filmmaking.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:28.199
The motion capture technology as well as the
use of 3D definitely had an impact on the

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:29.199
film industry.

00:08:29.199 --> 00:08:33.450
Although 3D as a gimmick is dying down a bit
these days, motion capture, as well as new

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:37.870
advances in computer graphics and life-like
animation are more integral to filmmakers

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:38.870
than ever.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:42.880
It's those technological advancements that
will be the lasting legacy of "Avatar," as

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:47.630
well as Cameron's ability to bring action
and heart to some of his most elaborate worlds.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:53.420
Regardless of how the sequels fare, the original
ushered us into the new millennium of cinematic experiences.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:58.070
So it's exciting to imagine what's coming
next from Cameron and Pandora when the second

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.339
"Avatar" movie, "The Way of Water," debuts
in December 2022.

